            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nBoth 'mini.clue' and 'mini.pick' *require* at least three rows between tabline (not included) and command-line (not included): two for borders and one for content. This is a limitation of the fact that floating windows can not be properly drawn on top of command-line.\n\nI can reproduce 'mini.clue' not showing up if there are only two lines available. Yes, there is no submode and I'll look into that.\n\nThe 'mini.pick' displays an error (which is correct behavior), but it is not really informative. Will also take a look.",
